964	    // ANIMATION RATE LOD. The pose write, the three IK chains and the two foot
965	    // ground rays are the whole per-actor cost, and for an actor that cannot
966	    // reach a pixel this frame (see AiSystem._updateRelevance) they buy nothing.
967	    // Evaluate a third as often and hand the solver the accumulated dt, so the
968	    // stride phase, the recoil envelope and the reload timeline stay on the same
969	    // clock — nothing skates or slides when the actor becomes visible again, and
970	    // the frame it does become visible is always a full evaluation because
971	    // lodIrrelevant is false by then.
